-- A rule that starts itself again, whose duty opens at a time counted from a
-- fixed moment (AFTER ... OF ...): its deadline is then fixed too, so once it
-- is past, each new copy is already late, and L4 could not check that this
-- comes to an end. Beside it, the same rule with a window that opens a
-- number of days after each copy starts, which L4 can check. Described in
-- doc/reference/regulative/rules-that-start-themselves-again.md.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alex
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF `pay rent`

-- Warns: the duty opens at a time counted from a fixed moment.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`opens on day 2` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MUST `pay rent`
    AFTER 2 OF 0
    WITHIN 1
    LEST `opens on day 2`

-- No warning: the window opens 2 days after each copy starts.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`opens 2 days later` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MUST `pay rent`
    AFTER 2
    WITHIN 1
    LEST `opens 2 days later`
